{"resource":{"id":"rust-interview-questions","title":"Rust — Interview Questions","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Intermediate","readingTime":"35 min","pages":35,"lastUpdated":"May 2026","tags":["Programming","Rust","Systems"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"300+ interview questions across beginner, intermediate, senior, and systems programming — with model answers."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Beginner (Q1-30)"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Ownership & Borrowing"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Lifetimes"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Traits & Generics"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Smart Pointers"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Concurrency"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Async"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Memory Safety"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Systems Programming"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Coding Problems"},{"id":"s11","label":"11. Senior/Staff"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Rust — Practice Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"21 min"},{"title":"Rust — Answer Key","tag":"Programming","time":"26 min"},{"title":"Rust — Complete Tutorial","tag":"Programming","time":"41 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Cover the full Rust interview landscape end to end.</li>\n          <li>Rehearse model answers you'd actually give in a room.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-sky-500/40 bg-sky-500/10 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 16v-4\"/><path d=\"M12 8h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">How to use</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Read the question, answer aloud, only then read the model answer.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Beginner</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"What is Rust?\">A systems language with memory safety enforced at compile time — no null, no data races, no GC.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"Difference between let and const?\"><code>let</code> is a runtime binding (default immutable); <code>const</code> is a compile-time constant with an explicit type.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"What is a crate?\">Rust's compilation and distribution unit — a binary or library.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"What does Cargo do?\">Manages projects, dependencies, builds, tests, docs, benchmarks.</QA>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Rust interview topic map: syntax → ownership → concurrency → systems.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Ownership &amp; Borrowing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Explain ownership.\">Each value has exactly one owner; on move, the source becomes invalid; on scope exit, drop runs.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"Move vs Copy?\">Copy types (integers, bools, small tuples) are duplicated by value; non-Copy types move.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"Explain the borrow-checker in one sentence.\">Aliasing XOR mutation — any number of shared borrows or exactly one mutable borrow.</QA>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Lifetimes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"What is a lifetime?\">A compile-time label for the region during which a reference is valid.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"What does 'static mean?\">Reference valid for the whole program.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"When to annotate?\">When the compiler can't infer relationships between multiple input/output references.</QA>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Traits &amp; Generics</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Traits vs interfaces?\">Traits support default methods, associated types, and are used for generic bounds — closer to Haskell type classes.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"Static vs dynamic dispatch?\">Static (monomorphized) is faster but generates more code; dynamic (<code>dyn Trait</code>) is smaller but adds one vtable indirection.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"Object safety?\">A trait is object-safe when it can be turned into a trait object (no <code>Self</code> in return position, no generics in methods).</QA>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Smart Pointers</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Box vs Rc vs Arc?\">Box: single owner; Rc: multi-owner single-threaded; Arc: multi-owner thread-safe.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"Interior mutability?\"><code>Cell</code>/<code>RefCell</code> (single-threaded) or <code>Mutex</code>/<code>RwLock</code> (multi-threaded).</QA>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Concurrency</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Send vs Sync?\">Send: safe to move across threads. Sync: safe to share (<code>&amp;T</code>) across threads.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"Why is Rc not Send?\">Non-atomic reference counting would race.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"Prevent deadlocks?\">Consistent lock order; use <code>parking_lot</code> or channels; avoid holding a lock across <code>.await</code>.</QA>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Async</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Why is a Future lazy?\">Nothing happens until it's polled — enables composition without allocation.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"tokio::spawn vs .await?\"><code>spawn</code> runs concurrently; <code>.await</code> waits sequentially.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"Pinning?\">Prevents self-referential structs from moving in memory — required for async state machines.</QA>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Async state machine: Poll → Pending/Ready → Wake.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Memory Safety</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"How does Rust prevent data races?\">Send/Sync markers + the borrow checker: shared XOR mutable.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"What is unsafe for?\">FFI, raw pointers, hardware, and building safe abstractions on top.</QA>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Systems Programming</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Zero-cost abstractions?\">High-level constructs compile down to the same code you'd write by hand.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"FFI with C?\"><code>extern \"C\"</code> + <code>#[repr(C)]</code>. Cross carefully; unsafe surface.</QA>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Coding Problems</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>// Reverse a string (bytes-safe for ASCII).\nfn reverse(s: &amp;str) -&gt; String { s.chars().rev().collect() }</code></pre></div>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>// Parallel sum with rayon.\nuse rayon::prelude::*;\nlet n: i64 = (1..=1_000_000).into_par_iter().sum();</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Senior / Staff</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <QA q=\"Design a lock-free queue?\">Discuss <code>crossbeam</code>'s Michael-Scott queue, ABA problem, memory ordering.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"Reduce compile times?\">Split crates, use <code>cargo build --timings</code>, generics discipline, <code>sccache</code>.</QA>\n        <QA q=\"When would you not use Rust?\">Prototypes, scripts, teams new to systems programming, tight-deadline UIs.</QA>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Interviews test taste as much as syntax. Have opinions, back them with trade-offs.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Live coding?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes — practice on a shared editor with types.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>Object safety</strong> — trait property allowing trait objects.</li>\n          <li><strong>NLL</strong> — Non-Lexical Lifetimes.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Interview guidance for educational use.</p>\n      </div></section>"}